    "available_at": "2026-11-15T16:46:40.051954+00:00",
    "body": "EICMA 2026 • Honda Africa Twin Gets Biggest Refresh in a Decade, They Now Call It CRF1150L\nDebrecen Plant Starts 2027 BMW iX4 Production in Hungary\n22 photos\nPhoto: BMW\nBMW's Hungarian vehicle plant has recently started production of the second Neue Klasse model assembled in Debrecen. iX4 is what the Bavarian automaker calls the coupe-ified sport utility vehicle, and its name alone is enough to understand that it's closely related to the more SUV-like iX3.\nIts introduction followed a very quick production ramp-up for the iX3, with BMW Group Plant Debrecen introducing round-the-clock manufacturing in September 2026 due to rising demand for the less expensive battery-electric model. In the first instance, iX4 customers will be presented with the 40 xDrive and 50 xDrive variants of the zero-emission sport utility vehicle.\nTo be launched in Europe this coming spring, the iX4 will also be offered in M Performance flavor. The upcoming M60 xDrive should drop next year as well, packing more than 600 horsepower and precisely 645 pound-feet (875 Newton-meters) of twist in optimal conditions.\nBMW Group Plant Debrecen reached a very important milestone back in July 2026 with the 50,000th unit of the iX3, the factory accomplishing this in less than a year. The German automaker reported more than 100,000 customer orders from European markets alone, hence the introduction of the third shift in September 2026.\nMore than 2 billion euros were invested by the company in the Debrecen complex, which occupies just around 400 hectares (988 acres) and targets 150,000 vehicles per annum. Building on the iX3, the iX4 distinguishes itself from the B-pillars back, flaunting a sloping roofline and a more dynamic rear end, liftgate and all. In 50 xDrive flavor, it promises up to 828 kilometers (514 miles) of WLTP range.\nPhoto: BMW That's marginally better than the iX3 50 xDrive, with both models benefiting from sixth-generation eDrive technology that includes cylindrical battery cells instead of the old prismatic design. Those in the market for the iX4 50 xDrive are presented with a very respectable 463 horsepower and 645 Newton-meters (476 pound-feet), along with 108.7 kilowatt-hours of high-voltage battery capacity.\nIts dual-motor setup enables a 0-100 sprint of 4.9 seconds, which is approximately 4.7 seconds from zero to 60 miles per hour. Like its brother, the iX4 is much obliged to support 400-kW fast charging on direct current, making it a tremendously good electric vehicle for long-distance driving.\nA 10-minute charging session can replenish up to 387 kilometers (240 miles) of WLTP range, but even in less-than-optimal conditions, the fast-charging system ensures that its battery will be sufficiently replenished in the time needed to enjoy a cup of coffee and a snack. Downgrading to the iX4 40 xDrive means 369 horsepower and 384 pound-feet (520 Newton-meters) of torque.\nIts driving range and maximum DC charging capability slot below the 50 as well, with BMW quoting 638 kilometers (396 miles) and 300 kilowatts at most. At the other end of the spectrum, the M60 is a dual-motor affair that tops 777 kilometers (483 miles) on a full charge. Debrecen handles high-voltage battery assembly for all three, alongside stamping, painting, and final assembly.\nThe front and rear motors for both launch versions, however, come from Austria. BMW's Steyr plant is tasked with producing said motors, which are shared with the more affordable iX3 40 xDrive and iX3 50 xDrive.\nLiked the article? Follow us to see more stories from autoevolution in your Google feeds.\n2027 bmw ix4 2028 BMW iX4 BMW iX4 BMW production EV\nRead Press Release\nAbout the author: Mircea Panait\nAfter a 1:43 scale model of a Ferrari 250 GTO sparked Mircea's interest for cars when he was a kid, an early internship at Top Gear sealed his career path. He's most interested in muscle cars and American trucks, but he takes a passing interest in quirky kei cars as well. Full profile\nUP NEXT Once Revolutionary, this 20-Year-Old American Yacht Is Now Asking for $20M",
